ready: 1
kind: rule
id: appraisal.rule.segment
display_id: RULE-APPRAISAL-SEGMENT
module: appraisal
title: Where one episode ends and the next begins
summary: >-
  A message from the person starts a new episode unless it is feedback on the agent's last turn;
  an episode closes when the next task starts, the session ends, or the session goes idle.
inputs:
  - name: events
    source: "A session's events not yet in an episode, in order"
    source_kind: stored
constants:
  - appraisal.const.markers
  - capture.const.episode-idle-close
decision:
  nodes:
    - {id: in, node_kind: input, text: The next message from the person}
    - {id: reply, node_kind: decision, text: Does it answer a question the agent's last message asked?}
    - {id: open, node_kind: decision, text: "Does it open with a correction, frustration, or praise phrase?"}
    - {id: short, node_kind: decision, text: Is it short and does it refer back to the agent's last turn without asking for anything new?}
    - {id: fb, node_kind: outcome, text: Feedback that stays in the current episode}
    - {id: task, node_kind: outcome, text: A new task that closes the current episode and starts the next}
  edges:
    - {from: in, to: reply}
    - {from: reply, to: fb, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: reply, to: open, label: "No"}
    - {from: open, to: fb, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: open, to: short, label: "No"}
    - {from: short, to: fb, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: short, to: task, label: "No"}
constraints:
  - text: Interrupts stay in the current episode
    hard: true
  - text: A directive phrase alone never makes a message feedback, because new requests often contain words such as always, never, or remember
    hard: true
  - text: The last open episode closes at a session end event or after the idle close time with no new records
    hard: true
default: A new task
rationale: >-
  The person's reaction to a piece of work usually arrives in their next message, so feedback
  belongs to the episode it reacts to and an episode stays open until the session moves on.
  Markers are anchored to the start of a message because ordinary requests are full of words like
  don't and always that would otherwise merge new tasks into old episodes.
